packages/coding-agent/README.md:10:lunR is a terminal coding agent derived from [pi](https://github.com/badlogic/pi-mono). It ships with interactive TUI, print/JSON, RPC, and SDK modes, plus baked-in MCP, subagents, permissions, plan mode, todos, cron, and a Telegram/Discord gateway.
packages/coding-agent/README.md:23:- [Sessions](#sessions)
packages/coding-agent/README.md:71:First-run optional features (Telegram/Discord gateway):
packages/coding-agent/README.md:82:lunr uninstall --purge   # also wipe ~/.lunr/agent (settings, credentials, sessions)
packages/coding-agent/README.md:90:Then just talk to lunR. By default it gives the model four tools: `read`, `write`, `edit`, and `bash`. `grep`, `find`, and `ls` exist but start off. Add more via [skills](#skills), [prompt templates](#prompt-templates), [extensions](#extensions), or [packages](#packages). See [built-in features](docs/features.md) for MCP, subagents, plan mode, cron, and the gateway.
packages/coding-agent/README.md:117:**API keys:** Anthropic, Ant Ling, OpenAI, Azure OpenAI, DeepSeek, NVIDIA NIM, Google Gemini, Google Vertex, Amazon Bedrock, Mistral, Groq, Cerebras, Cloudflare AI Gateway, Cloudflare Workers AI, xAI, OpenRouter, Vercel AI Gateway, ZAI Coding Plan, OpenCode Zen/Go, Hugging Face, Fireworks, Together AI, Kimi For Coding, MiniMax, Xiaomi MiMo, Qwen Token Plan.
packages/coding-agent/README.md:134:- **Footer** - Working directory, git branch, session name, token/cache usage, cost, context usage, plan bar, current model. Customize its segments under `/settings` → Customize.
packages/coding-agent/README.md:169:| `/goal` | Session goal (forces session auto permission mode) |
packages/coding-agent/README.md:170:| `/processes` | Background processes started this session |
packages/coding-agent/README.md:171:| `/usage` | This-session token totals, context, and every stored subscription plan |
packages/coding-agent/README.md:174:| `/resume`, `/sessions` | Pick from previous sessions |
packages/coding-agent/README.md:175:| `/new` | Start a new session |
packages/coding-agent/README.md:176:| `/name`, `/title` | Set session display name |
packages/coding-agent/README.md:177:| `/session` | Show session info |
packages/coding-agent/README.md:178:| `/tree` | Jump to any point in the session (`ctrl+o` cycles filters) |
packages/coding-agent/README.md:179:| `/undo`, `/edit`, `/redo` | Same-session rewind; `/edit` pastes the last prompt |
packages/coding-agent/README.md:182:| `/fork` | Create a new session from a previous user message |
packages/coding-agent/README.md:187:| `/export [file]` | Export session to HTML or JSONL |
packages/coding-agent/README.md:188:| `/import <file>` | Import and resume a JSONL session |
packages/coding-agent/README.md:189:| `/share` | Upload as a private GitHub gist (HTML viewer still defaults to https://pi.dev/session/ — leftover, not lunR-hosted) |
packages/coding-agent/README.md:208:| Escape twice within 500ms | Stop this session's active async subagents; otherwise open `/tree` when idle |
packages/coding-agent/README.md:233:## Sessions
packages/coding-agent/README.md:235:Sessions are stored as JSONL files with a tree structure. Each entry has an `id` and `parentId`, enabling in-place branching without creating new files. See [docs/session-format.md](docs/session-format.md) for file format.
packages/coding-agent/README.md:239:Sessions auto-save to `~/.lunr/agent/sessions/` organized by working directory.
